{
  "rules": [
    "Model forecasts exhibit a persistent upward bias relative to true outcomes, consistently predicting higher prices than realized.",
    "Forecasts show significant lag in reacting to recent price spikes; the model fails to incorporate immediate volatility or momentum shifts seen in the last 3-5 days of history.",
    "When sentiment history contains mixed signals (e.g., positive and negative values within a short window), the model tends to smooth these out, resulting in an oversmoothed trajectory that misses sharp reversals.",
    "The model demonstrates a failure to account for mean reversion after rapid price increases; it extrapolates upward trends linearly rather than recognizing the likelihood of a correction back to historical averages.",
    "In scenarios where the last 3 days show high volatility or a spike followed by a drop, the model's forecast remains flat or slowly rising, failing to capture the subsequent downward pressure in true outcomes."
  ]
}
